    {
      "t": "h2",
      "v": "1. CSS Functions"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "v": "CSS functions are used to dynamically compute property values, making styling more flexible and scalable."
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "attr()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Retrieves an attribute value from an HTML element and inserts it into the stylesheet.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "a::after {\r\n  content: \" (\" attr(href) \")\";\r\n}"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Useful for adding dynamic content from HTML attributes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "calc()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Performs calculations directly in CSS.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "width: calc(100% - 50px);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Helps create responsive designs with precise measurements."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "clamp()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Defines a value between a minimum, preferred, and maximum range.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 3rem);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Ensures text remains readable across different screen sizes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "max() & min()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Returns the maximum or minimum value among given values.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "width: max(300px, 50%);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Useful for setting adaptive layouts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "var()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Used to declare and use CSS variables.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": ":root {\r\n  --primary-color: #ff6600;\r\n}\r\nbody {\r\n  background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n}"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Enables theming and reuse of values."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "v": "2. CSS Color Manipulation"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "v": "CSS provides several functions to manipulate colors dynamically."
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "hsl()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Defines colors using Hue, Saturation, and Lightness.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "color: hsl(200, 50%, 50%);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Makes color adjustments more intuitive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "rgba()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Defines colors with an alpha (transparency) value.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "background-color: rgba(255, 0, 0, 0.5);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Allows fine-tuned opacity control."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "invert()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Inverts colors for a negative effect.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "filter: invert(100%);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Useful for dark mode toggles."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "saturate()"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
        "Adjusts the color saturation.",
        "Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "filter: saturate(200%);"
    },
    {
      "t": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "v": [
