    },
    {
      "t": "h2",
      "v": "FAQs"
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "1. How do CSS filters work?"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "v": "CSS filters apply effects like blur, brightness, and contrast to elements. They are commonly used on images but can be applied to any HTML element."
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "2. What is the difference between rgba() and hsl()?"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "v": "rgba() defines colors using red, green, blue, and alpha (opacity). hsl() uses hue, saturation, and lightness, making it easier to create color variations."
    },
    {
      "t": "h3",
      "v": "3. When should I use calc() in CSS?"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "v": "Use calc() when you need to dynamically calculate CSS values, such as setting flexible margins or padding that adjusts based on viewport size."
    }
  ]
}
